   "text": "I read this as a PROTAC-type molecule with three parts joined in sequence: an aminopyridazine\u2013phenol ligand, a PEG linker, and a VHL-type hydroxyproline ligand.\n\n**Left end.** A pyridazine carries an NH2 and, on the carbon next to a ring nitrogen, a 2-hydroxyphenyl group. Its remaining ring carbon is bonded to the C4 of a pyrazole.\n\n**Linker.** The pyrazole N1 is bonded to a chain with five ether oxygens: N\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O. The last oxygen is bonded to C3 of an isoxazole.\n\n**Isoxazole to VHL ligand.** The isoxazole C5 is bonded to a CH that carries an isopropyl group and a C(=O) attached to the pyrrolidine nitrogen. The pyrrolidine is a 4-hydroxyproline whose C2 carries a C(=O)NH\u2013CH2\u2013aryl amide. The aryl is a para-substituted phenyl bearing a 4-methylthiazol-5-yl group.\n\n**Stereochemistry.**\n- The isopropyl-bearing CH has the isopropyl on a hashed bond. Its CIP priorities are C(=O) > isoxazole C5 > isopropyl > H, which gives S.\n- Hydroxyproline: I took the hashed OH and wedged carboxamide as the standard VHL (2S,4R) configuration rather than re-deriving each centre from the drawing.\n\nSMILES: Nc1nnc(-c2ccccc2O)cc1-c1cnn(c1)CCOCCOCCOCCOCCOc1cc(on1)[C@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N1C[C@H](O)C[C@H]1C(=O)NCc1ccc(cc1)-c1scnc1C"
